            <ArticleTitle>Systolic coronary occlusion due to myocardial bridging--a rare cause of ischaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial bridging causing systolic occlusion of the left anterior descending coronary artery was identified in a 47-year-old man with angina. A fixed anterolateral wall defect was demonstrated on thallium imaging and he underwent successful division of the bridge resulting in abolition of his symptoms and disappearance of the thallium defect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
